From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:35:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 084/274] TileLang V4.1 mHC: the stream projection at FP32
 precision

The projection of the BF16 streams on the FP32 fn ran on TF32 tensor cores,
which keep 11 of fn's 24 significant bits. Each fn value is now split exactly
into three TF32-representable parts and the three GEMMs accumulate in FP32,
so every product is exact, as DeepSeek's reference computes the mixes in FP32.

(cherry picked from commit dfc3827e3598064f3c7b33afc1c4a18db70cd7cc)

